{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"agent_message","text":"The corrected prompt instruction is now a valid behavioral baseline—and it performs poorly: it does not consistently reduce detector scores, but it sharply changes content (embedding Δ −0.505) and raises 3-gram repetition (+0.212). This reinforces the matched-quality requirement: “write like a human” is not a clean substitute for activation intervention here. The main conclusion remains a causal negative result at tested doses, with low power for small effects. I’m now assembling the report and running leakage/reproducibility checks."}}
